# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pair - local configuration
#
# This file is COMMITTED, which is unusual and worth explaining rather than
# quietly getting on with.
#
# A Firebase *client* configuration is not a secret. It contains a project id,
# an app id and an API key, and all three of them ship inside the APK where
# anyone can read them with nothing more than `unzip`. The API key is not a
# password to a room: Firebase restricts it server-side by package name and
# signing certificate, so a key lifted from this file is useless against any
# other app. Firebase's own documentation permits client configs in source
# control, and every Firebase Android SDK behaves this way.
#
# So the practical effect of hiding it would be zero protection and a broken
# clone. The real protection is rotating the key, and restricting it by package
# and SHA-1 in the Firebase console.
#
# What is genuinely secret, and IS gitignored: `local.properties` (your SDK
# path), the release signing keys, and anything added to `.env.local`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Firebase project ------------------------------------------------------
# Must match `.firebaserc` and `app/google-services.json`.
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=pair-4791e
FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL=https://pair-4791e-default-rtdb.asia-southeast1.firebasedatabase.app

# --- Android application identity -----------------------------------------
# Must match the manifest's `applicationId`, or FCM token registration is
# rejected at runtime.
ANDROID_PACKAGE_NAME=com.wood.pair

# --- Build -----------------------------------------------------------------
# `google-services.json` is the file the Google Services Gradle plugin actually
# reads. There is no code path in this app that parses this one: an Android app
# has no environment to read it from at runtime, and threading a .env parser in
# to do so would only move the same public values somewhere less conventional.
# This file is therefore documentation and a single place to change them.
GOOGLE_SERVICES_FILE=app/google-services.json
